# Deny by default, then name what the image needs. The Dockerfile copies four
# things, so those are the four exceptions.
#
# An allowlist rather than a list of exclusions, for the same reason the policy
# layer works that way: a new directory added to the repo is excluded by
# default rather than silently joining the build context. `local/` holds
# pricing, strategy and design notes, and `artifacts/` and `benchmarks/` are
# over 1.8G between them; none of it belongs anywhere near an image.
#
# BuildKit already sends only the files a COPY needs, so today this changes
# nothing. It matters for the classic builder, for a remote or CI builder where
# the context crosses a network, and for the day someone writes `COPY . .`.
*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src
